  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "${(1+5z)}^{8}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=5z$ and $n=8$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+5z)}^{8} & =1+8\\cdot 5z+\\frac{8(8-1)}{2!}\\cdot {(5z)}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+40z+\\frac{8\\cdot 7}{2}\\cdot 25{z}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+40z+28\\cdot 25{z}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+40z+700{z}^{2}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
